{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexSubstitutionScale","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Add","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.candidateRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.candidateRatio","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The ratio whose non-constancy is the content of `no_constant_rescaling`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.candidateCoupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.candidateCoupling","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L83-L86","doc":"The order-matched candidate coupling `(W − W(1)) · ℏ_q`, which vanishes to\nsecond order at `q = 1` exactly as `s²` does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L80-L81","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`, the corpus's order-`(q−1)` bridge factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_one","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L74-L76","doc":"`s²(1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_eq_twoQ_sub_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_eq_twoQ_sub_two","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**The single-crossing coupling is a classical-value deviation.**\n`s² = (q^{1/2} − q^{-1/2})² = [2]_q − [2]_1`.  This is an identity, not a\nnormalisation choice, and it is why the decay rate vanishes at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.twoQ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.twoQ_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L62-L64","doc":"`[2]_1 = 2`: the classical value of the fundamental dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.twoQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.twoQ","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The `SU_q(2)` fundamental quantum dimension `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}